	<item>
		<title>Comment on Alliancism by RobW42</title>
		<link>http://civgene.matthewnewhall.com/archives/1261#comment-86</link>
		<dc:creator>RobW42</dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 09 May 2016 15:27:08 +0000</pubDate>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://civgene.matthewnewhall.com/?p=1261#comment-86</guid>
		<description><![CDATA[I appreciate your writing, and definitely recognize the &quot;Alliancism to Fascism&quot; thing as a reality.  I sometimes see myself going that direction, save for the fact that i have no alliances and practically no friendships.  

Myself, and others who you might classify as psychopaths, may have been overly empathic earlier in life, and perhaps felt too much emotional pain for one reason or another, and had to shut it down as a survival technique.  Perhaps the harsh realities of life (some of which are random, in theory) create that type of person.  Perhaps in my case, medicine which is designed to shut down emotions (or minimize the experience of them) leads to the creation of psychopathic personality traits.   

These are just thoughts, not arguments.]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>I appreciate your writing, and definitely recognize the &#8220;Alliancism to Fascism&#8221; thing as a reality.  I sometimes see myself going that direction, save for the fact that i have no alliances and practically no friendships.  </p>
<p>Myself, and others who you might classify as psychopaths, may have been overly empathic earlier in life, and perhaps felt too much emotional pain for one reason or another, and had to shut it down as a survival technique.  Perhaps the harsh realities of life (some of which are random, in theory) create that type of person.  Perhaps in my case, medicine which is designed to shut down emotions (or minimize the experience of them) leads to the creation of psychopathic personality traits.   </p>
<p>These are just thoughts, not arguments.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
